1
00:04:55,555 --> 00:05:01,555
In this clean, orderly, disciplined world, who
needs guys like McMurphy? Everybody.

2
00:09:51,111 --> 00:09:57,111
One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest is a drama film directed by Miloš Forman.

3
00:14:46,666 --> 00:14:52,666
A petty criminal fakes insanity to serve his sentence
in a mental ward rather than prison.

4
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:48,222
He soon finds himself as a leader to the other patients—and an enemy
to the cruel, domineering nurse who runs the ward.

5
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:43,777
Randle Patrick McMurphy, played by Jack Nicholson.

6
00:29:33,333 --> 00:29:39,333
Billy Bibbit, played by Brad Dourif.

7
00:34:28,888 --> 00:34:34,888
Nurse Mildred Ratched, played by Louise Fletcher.

8
00:39:24,444 --> 00:39:30,444
Martini, played by Danny DeVito.

9
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:26,000
Dale Harding, played by William Redfield.

10
00:49:15,555 --> 00:49:21,555
Orderly Turkle, played by Scatman Crothers.

11
00:54:11,111 --> 00:54:17,111
One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest is a 1975 American psychological comedy-drama film
directed by Miloš Forman, based on the 1962 novel of the same name by Ken Kesey.

12
00:59:06,666 --> 00:59:12,666
The film stars Jack Nicholson as a new patient at a mental
institution and Louise Fletcher as the abusive head nurse.

13
01:04:02,222 --> 01:04:08,222
Will Sampson, Danny DeVito, Sydney Lassick, William Redfield, Christopher Lloyd, and Brad
Dourif play supporting roles, with the latter two making their feature-film debuts.

14
01:08:57,777 --> 01:09:03,777
Originally announced in 1962 with Kirk Douglas
starring, the film took 13 years to develop.

15
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
Filming finally began in January 1975 and lasted three months, on location in Salem,
Oregon, and the surrounding area, and in Depoe Bay on the north Oregon coast.

16
01:18:48,888 --> 01:18:54,888
The producers shot the film in the Oregon State Hospital, an actual
psychiatric hospital, which is also the novel's setting.

17
01:23:44,444 --> 01:23:50,444
The hospital is still in operation, though the original
buildings in the film have been demolished.

18
01:28:40,000 --> 01:28:46,000
The film was released on November 19, 1975.

19
01:33:35,555 --> 01:33:41,555
One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest received critical acclaim and is considered by
critics and audiences to be one of the greatest films ever made.

20
01:38:31,111 --> 01:38:37,111
It is the second of three films to win all five major Academy Awards (Best Picture, Best Actor, Best Actress, Best Director, and
Best Adapted Screenplay) following It Happened One Night (1934) and preceding 1991's The Silence of the Lambs.

21
01:43:26,666 --> 01:43:32,666
It won numerous Golden Globe and BAFTA Awards.

22
01:48:22,222 --> 01:48:28,222
In 1993, the film was deemed "culturally, historically, or aesthetically significant" by the United
States Library of Congress and selected for preservation in the National Film Registry.

23
01:53:17,777 --> 01:53:23,777
Additionally, One Flew Over the Cuckoo's Nest was ranked number 33 on
the American Film Institute's updated 100 Years...

24
01:58:13,333 --> 01:58:19,333
100 Movies list in 2007.

25
02:03:08,888 --> 02:03:14,888
The film explores themes of mentally disabled, friendship,
based on novel or book, nurse, lunatic asylum.

26
02:08:04,444 --> 02:08:10,444
The tone is emotional.
